| – **Existentialism (Sartre, Camus)** | No predetermined meaning; we must create our own. | By making authentic choices, taking responsibility, and embracing freedom. |
| – **Absurdism (Camus)** | Life is inherently meaningless, but we can revolt against that by finding personal meaning. | Engaging in creative work, love, or rebellion against the absurd. |
| – **Humanism** | Meaning comes from human values—reason, compassion, creativity. | Building relationships, pursuing knowledge, improving society. |
| **Scientific / Evolutionary** | No ultimate purpose, but life “means” what we assign it through our biology and culture. | Using science to enhance well‑being, understanding our place in the universe. |
