| **Hash** | A fixed‑size digital fingerprint produced by a cryptographic one‑way function. Changing even a single bit in a block changes its hash dramatically. |
| **Previous‑block hash** | Each block includes the hash of the block that came before it, creating a chain. |
| **Nonce (or proof‑of‑stake “stake”)** | A number that miners (or validators) adjust to satisfy the network’s **consensus rule** (e.g., find a hash below a target). |
| **Node** | A computer that keeps a copy of the entire blockchain, validates transactions/blocks, and communicates with other nodes. |
| **Consensus mechanism** | The protocol by which all nodes agree on a single version of the ledger (e.g., Proof‑of‑Work, Proof‑of‑Stake). |
| **Digital signatures** | Asymmetric‑key cryptography (public‑private key pairs) that proves a transaction was authorized by the owner of the funds. |

