A blockchain is a **distributed, tamper‑evident ledger** that records transactions (or any data) across many computers (called *nodes*) so that the record cannot be altered retroactively without the consensus of the network.  

Below is a step‑by‑step walkthrough of how most public blockchains (e.g., Bitcoin, Ethereum) work.

---

## 1. The basic data structure – a “block”

| Field | Purpose |
